+V. Experiments
+
+Evaluation setting. The evaluation uses CIFAR-100 and the 100-class CIFAR-ResNet18 [13], with the fixed final
+dense checkpoint as the pruning parent. Each method targets 2:4 sparsity in the same eligible internal convolutional
+layers. Dense training uses 200 epochs. The stem, classifier, BN parameters, and biases remain dense.
+
+A. Post-training endpoints
+
+Table 1 provides the existing reference accuracies and the evaluation slot for APBR-guided conditional OBS. The
+SAM reference applies a magnitude mask, and Wanda [10] uses activation-aware scores; both are mask-only endpoints.
+SparseGPT [11] includes its native selection and OBS compensation. The pending APBR-SAM evaluation will follow
+the geometry-first and conditional-second procedure in Algorithm 1, including joint compensation.
+
