+
+The protocol uses the official CIFAR-100 training and test splits with 50,000 and 10,000 images, respectively. The
+dense parent is the fixed final checkpoint after 200 epochs. All methods use the same 19 eligible internal Conv2d layers,
+output-row-contiguous OIHW groups, and dense incomplete tails. The input stem, classifier, BN affine parameters,
+and biases are excluded from pruning.
+
+    The geometry-first evaluation uses the matched dense weights and log-scales, fixed training calibration identities,
+and frozen reconstruction settings. Calibration and pruning retain the dense parent’s BN buffers. After all masks and
+compensated checkpoints are frozen, each final artifact is evaluated once on the test split. No recovery training is
+included. The accuracy slots for this method are marked PENDING in Section V.
+
+    At each group entrance, the current physical weights include updates committed by preceding groups. The active
+inverse in Eq. (8) is recomputed mathematically for the remaining free coordinates; its shared Cholesky-tail represen-
+tation avoids a separate inverse for each output row. All exact selection ties use the lower stored coordinate index.
+After the selected pair is compensated, the full quartet is frozen before advancing.
