-\end{table}
-
-SAM and Wanda retain $55.54\pm1.36\%$ and $56.48\pm3.83\%$ with mask application alone. SparseGPT retains $77.26\pm0.42\%$ after its native dynamic selection and OBS compensation. APBR-SAM reaches $77.63\pm0.28\%$ after conditional selection and one joint OBS compensation from the unmodified current weights. The APBR-SAM row is based on two rather than three seeds, so the $0.37$-point difference from SparseGPT is exploratory rather than a formal ranking.
-
-\subsection{Ablation study}
-We next compare the same conditional-greedy selection and joint OBS compensation after SAM and APBR-SAM dense training. This changes the dense parent and, for APBR-SAM, activates the learned geometric tie-break; it therefore tests the complete training-to-pruning path rather than isolating a single causal component.
