+\section{Experiments}\label{sec:experiments}
+\paragraph{Evaluation setting.}
+The evaluation uses CIFAR-100 and the 100-class CIFAR-ResNet18~\cite{resnet}, with the fixed final dense checkpoint as the pruning parent. Each method targets 2:4 sparsity in the same eligible internal convolutional layers. Dense training uses 200 epochs. The stem, classifier, BN parameters, and biases remain dense.
+
+\subsection{Post-training endpoints}
+Table~\ref{tab:main} provides the existing reference accuracies and the evaluation slot for APBR-guided conditional OBS. The SAM reference applies a magnitude mask, and Wanda~\cite{wanda} uses activation-aware scores; both are mask-only endpoints. SparseGPT~\cite{sparsegpt} includes its native selection and OBS compensation. The pending APBR-SAM evaluation will follow the geometry-first and conditional-second procedure in Algorithm~\ref{alg:apbr}, including joint compensation.
+
+\begin{table}[H]\centering
+\caption{CIFAR-100 post-pruning accuracy. Completed reference rows retain their existing three-seed mean $\pm$ sample SD. PENDING denotes the evaluation of the geometry-first method defined in this paper.}\label{tab:main}
+\begin{tabular}{lc}
+\toprule
+Method & Accuracy (\%) \\
+\midrule
+SAM & $55.54\pm1.36$ \\
+Wanda & $56.48\pm3.83$ \\
+SparseGPT & $77.26\pm0.42$ \\
+APBR-SAM & PENDING \\
+\bottomrule
+\end{tabular}
+\end{table}
+
+The reference results identify reconstruction as an important part of the post-training endpoint: SAM and Wanda report $55.54\pm1.36\%$ and $56.48\pm3.83\%$ after mask application, while native SparseGPT reports $77.26\pm0.42\%$ after selection and compensation. The APBR evaluation combines support selection with reconstruction and measures its accuracy at the same post-pruning stage, without recovery training.
+
+\subsection{Geometry-guided selection}
+The mechanism comparison uses the same APBR dense parent, calibration inputs, damping, processing order, and joint compensation. The physical conditional-OBS control chooses its first deletion by singleton OBS cost. APBR-guided conditional OBS instead chooses it by the saved geometry score. Both then select the second position in the virtual conditional state. This comparison directly tests the role of the initial geometric decision.
+
+\begin{table}[H]\centering
+\caption{Planned same-parent comparison of the initial deletion rule. Both rows use conditional OBS for the second deletion and the same joint compensation.}\label{tab:ablation}
+\begin{tabular}{lc}
+\toprule
+Initial deletion rule & Accuracy (\%) \\
+\midrule
+Physical singleton OBS & PENDING \\
+APBR geometry & PENDING \\
+\bottomrule
+\end{tabular}
+\end{table}
+
+The evaluation will record mask agreement, physical layer-output reconstruction error, and final classification accuracy. Mask agreement locates changes in the selected support; reconstruction error measures their layer-level effect; classification accuracy measures the resulting network endpoint. Before evaluation, the resulting masks and compensated checkpoints will be frozen for a single final test.
